WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.023
Jakarta, 2025: nearly 42 million people,
the largest city in the world by the

2
00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.390
UN's count.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:14.450
On the same count, there were 8 megacities
of 10 million people or more in 1975.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.690
By 2025, there were 33.

5
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.590
But what counts as urban?

6
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.450
In Denmark, 200 people can be enough.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.050
In Japan, it takes 50,000.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.910
So how urban is the world, really?

9
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.410
In this mission, you'll learn
what makes a place urban:

10
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.150
its site, situation,
function and land use.

11
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.010
Then you'll climb the urban
hierarchy, test the rank-size rule,

12
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.670
and compare planned Brasília
with spontaneous growth.

13
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.590
Your mission: find out
how urban the world is,

14
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.310
and explain your answer.
